  "_comment": [
    "Closed-shell CCSD(T) reference energies for the native OpenQP path.",
    "Produced with PySCF (RHF conv_tol=1e-12, CCSD conv_tol=1e-11) on the same",
    "geometry and basis, then reproduced end-to-end through OpenQP's own Rys",
    "integral engine, cc_ao2mo transformation and cc_lib solver.",
    "",
    "cartesian=true marks the Pople sets, where OpenQP uses 6d Cartesian shells;",
    "PySCF needs gto.M(..., cart=True) to be compared against them.  Without it",
    "the two codes are running different basis sets (28 vs 30 functions for",
    "CO/6-31G*) and the correlation energies are not comparable.",
    "",
    "scf_reference is PySCF's RHF total energy.  The CC tolerances below only",
    "mean anything when OpenQP reproduces that number: a correlation energy is",
    "defined relative to its reference determinant."
